MODIFICATION MADE HERE
----------------------
Two module properties in altera_avalon_new_sdram_controller_hw.tcl are changed
from Intel's original, and the change is commented at the point it occurs:

    HIDE_FROM_SOPC      true -> false
    HIDE_FROM_QUARTUS   true -> false

Intel set both when retiring the IP from the Platform Designer catalog in 20.1,
so it remained instantiable for existing designs but was hidden from new ones.
They are false here so the component appears in the catalog and can be used,
which is the only reason to preserve it. Set them back to true for Intel's
original catalog behaviour.

Nothing else is altered: not the rest of the _hw.tcl, not the Perl generators,
and not the generated RTL.

WHAT IN THIS DIRECTORY IS *NOT* INTEL'S
---------------------------------------
Three things here are the repository author's own work and ARE covered by the
repository's MIT licence:

    example/        a DE10-Lite demonstration that instantiates the controller
    NOTICE          this file
    README.md       the component's documentation

The example contains no Intel source. It builds a Platform Designer system
around the controller and drives it from original RTL; Qsys generates Intel's
controller into the build tree at generation time, and that generated output
remains Intel's under the terms above.
